extends layout

block content
  .wrapper
    section
      .content
      //-
        h1 Welcome, exile.
        p A reckless war has caused the fabric of reality to shatter.
        p Reality only exists when observed.
        p Where reality is broken the world is covered in a veil of black dust.
        p Reality must be re-asserted by repairing the filaments that once bound it together.
        p This filament is called Tether.
        p Find Tether. Restore reality. Rebuild the world.
      -//
        h1 Welcome.
        p This is the demo of Black Dust, a browser strategy game that I started developing as my bachelors project.
        p This version features 1 unit class, the scout, which has two abilities.
        p It is multiplayer which means that you will be able to encounter other players that may have tried it out.
        p The game is built with node.js, express.js and socket.io for realtime client-server communication.
        p //Martin
        form#loginForm(method='post' action='/users/demologin')
          if !user
            p Please enter a user name.
            input#uid(type='text' name='uid' required placeholder="Name")
            button.button(type='submit') Submit
            if errors != undefined && errors.length != 0
              each error in errors
                div.error-msg(role='alert' id='a1') #{error.msg}
            if success_msg != ''
              div(role='alert' id='a2') #{success_msg}
            if error_msg != ''
              div.error-msg(role='alert' id='a3') #{error_msg}
            if error != ''
              div.error-msg(role='alert' id='a4') #{error}
          if user
            li
              a(href='/game') Enter the game

  .fade


    
